# B-586: Nested dict LGM slot alignment.
# Before the fix, the resolver used enter_scope(&keys, Dict) with offset=0 for
# nested dict literals. At runtime, eval_dict_core builds extended_group =
# outer_frame.group ++ letrec_slots, placing entries at outer_frame.group.len()+i.
# With offset=0, LGM(0) resolved to the first builtin (field-get), not the entry.
#
# Case 1: Nested dict in a document-level dict value, referencing outer sibling.
[x: 10
 inner: [ref: x  doubled: [* x 2]]]
[inner.ref  inner.doubled]
=== out
[0: 10  1: 20]
